    keyInsights: [`Brian Cox emphasizes the unpredictability of performance in film, stating that directors often cannot micromanage actors effectively.`, `Cox's directorial debut in 'Glen Rothen' taught him valuable lessons about leadership and collaboration on set.`, `He appreciates the influence of directors like Lindsay Anderson, who understand how to guide performances without overpowering actors.`, `Despite gaining sympathy for directors through his own experiences, Cox candidly acknowledges that many can still be quite egotistical and difficult.`],
